# Tips: what to do next. The first entry whose conditions hold is the current tip, so each act's
# list runs from its last step back to its first. Shown by the Tip button or H, and always on
# screen in tip mode.
#
# Two rungs: the nudge comes first, pointing at the person, place or idea without the answer;
# asking again for the same tip gives the plain line, which says exactly what to do. Tip mode
# shows the nudge until the player asks. The compass's look text (items.adv) nudges in
# character, at the same level.

# Act I
tip if act 1 and has licence and has manifest and ledger_read
  nudge "A licence, a manifest, and the ledger read with your own eyes. That was Bramwick's whole list."
  "You have everything. Give the licence to Bramwick in the customs house."
tip if act 1 and has licence and loft_open and not ledger_read
  nudge "The loft over the chandler's is open. Bramwick wanted the ledger read, not fetched."
  "Go up to the loft from Chandler's Lane and open the harbour ledger on the desk."
tip if act 1 and has licence and not ledger_read
  nudge "The berth stays Cray's until Bramwick has proof, and the proof starts in the harbour ledger. It's kept in the loft over the chandler's."
  "The harbour ledger is in the loft above the chandler's. Use the crowbar on the bolted shutter in Chandler's Lane."
tip if act 1 and has licence and not has manifest
  nudge "Bramwick wants the Arcadia's manifest. The chandler keeps a copy of every ship he provisions, and has been waiting three years to be paid."
  "The chandler keeps manifest copies. Use the harbour stamp on the spike of invoices on his counter."
tip if act 1 and has licence
  nudge "A licence is only paper until the Harbourmaster has read it."
  "Show Bramwick your licence: give it to him in the customs house."
tip if act 1 and has stamp and has licence_form
  nudge "A blank licence and the harbour stamp, in the same pocket. Any clerk of the house may stamp in the Harbourmaster's absence."
  "Use the harbour stamp on the licence form."
tip if act 1 and has stamp
  nudge "The stamp needs something to stamp. Bramwick keeps the blank licences where he can glare at them."
  "Pick up a blank licence form from Bramwick's desk."
tip if act 1 and has drawer_key
  nudge "Bramwick's key belongs in Bramwick's desk, where the harbour stamp lives."
  "Use the drawer key on Bramwick's drawer in the customs house."
tip if act 1 and has rum and knows_key
  nudge "Marta named her price for Bramwick's key, and it's in your pocket."
  "Give the inspected rum to Marta in the Salty Keel."
tip if act 1 and has rum
  nudge "Bramwick knows how a clerk gets a licence after the night bell. And somebody at the Keel is missing a bottle."
  "Ask Bramwick how a clerk could stamp a licence. Marta will want her rum."
tip if act 1 and knows_key and has crowbar
  nudge "Marta's rum is nailed up in a crate on the pier, waiting for customs to inspect it. You are customs."
  "Marta wants her rum. Use the crowbar on the impounded crate on the pier."
tip if act 1 and knows_key
  nudge "Marta will trade Bramwick's key for her rum, and customs is holding her rum on the pier, nailed shut."
  "Marta's rum is in the impounded crate on the pier. Pick up the crowbar by the bollard first."
tip if act 1
  nudge "The Marrow only takes licensed hands, and licences are the customs house's business."
  "Talk to Bramwick in the customs house (the stone building on the right) about signing on."
# Act II
tip if act 2 and vane_convinced
  nudge "Vane gave the orders: Quill takes the wheel, and you call the bearings from the bow. The compass knows the way."
  "Go forward to the bow (the foredeck, at the back of the main deck) and use the compass on the fog. Call the side the needle swings to."
tip if act 2 and quill_navigator and crew_agree
  nudge "A navigator and a crew. The third term is a reason Pell would have, and Pell left one, unfinished."
  "Give Pell's log to Captain Vane in her cabin."
tip if act 2 and has sextant and vane_terms
  nudge "Vane wants a navigator who'll swear to the line. Somebody on deck has been reading the stars for nothing."
  "Give Pell's sextant to Quill on the main deck."
tip if act 2 and vane_terms and dinner and not chest_open
  nudge "Hobb has left his post for the stew. Nobody is guarding Pell's chest."
  "Hobb has gone to dinner. Open Pell's sea-chest below decks."
tip if act 2 and vane_terms and dinner and not crew_agree
  nudge "Hobb won't sail south for money, only for blood. You're carrying twenty-two names."
  "Give the Arcadia's manifest to Hobb at the mess table below decks."
tip if act 2 and vane_terms and not dinner
  nudge "Hobb won't leave Pell's chest until dinner, and dinner waits on Dorrit, who serves nothing unstamped."
  "Go below decks (the hatch on the main deck). Use the harbour stamp on Dorrit's stew."
tip if act 2 and quill_helped
  nudge "The captain is in her cabin with her charts, and your compass disagrees with all of them."
  "Go up the quarterdeck steps, through the carved doors under the wheel, into the captain's cabin. Use the compass on her chart."
tip if act 2 and has spyglass
  nudge "Quill lost something on deck in the dark, and you've found it."
  "Talk to Quill, ask how to get past, and give her back her spyglass."
tip if act 2 and seen:quill.what
  nudge "Quill wants her spyglass back. She dropped it on this deck, somewhere in the dark."
  "Quill dropped her spyglass on deck. Look between the crates on the left."
tip if act 2
  nudge "The captain is aft, and the lookout is between you and aft."
  "Talk to Quill, the lookout: ask her how to get past to the captain."
# Act III
tip if act 3 and has flag16
  nudge "Vane is watching the wreck's masthead for a new flag, and you're holding one."
  "Cross the reef flats (left of the salt camp) to the wreck, and use flag sixteen on the halyard."
tip if act 3 and quill_free
  nudge "Three years, and he's standing in a salt pan. Say something."
  "Talk to your father, Ansel, in the salt camp."
tip if act 3 and form9
  nudge "There is a Form 9 now, stamped and in your hand. Pike lives for forms."
  "Give the Bill of Health (now Form 9) to Pike."
tip if act 3 and knows_form9
  nudge "A Form 9 is clean paper with a harbour stamp on it. The back of something will do."
  "Use the harbour stamp on the Bill of Health to write Form 9 on its back."
tip if act 3 and fog_down
  nudge "Quill is in the store hut, pending inspection, and Pike obeys any correctly completed form."
  "Talk to Pike in the salt camp and ask what would release Quill."
tip if act 3 and gate_open and has bucket_water
  nudge "The fog comes from the Weather Works, and you're carrying a bucket of lagoon."
  "Go through the gate to the Weather Works and use the bucket of lagoon on the great brazier."
tip if act 3 and gate_open and has bucket
  nudge "An empty bucket frightens nobody. There's a whole lagoon out there."
  "Fill the bucket at the lagoon (the shore or the wreck), then use it on the great brazier."
tip if act 3 and gate_open
  nudge "The great brazier makes the fog, and fire hates water. You'll need something to carry it in."
  "Pick up the bucket in the Arcadia's cabin and fill it at the lagoon."
tip if act 3 and has bill and bill_smoked and bill_stamped and bill_signed and bill_dated
  nudge "Fumigated, stamped, countersigned, dated. Pike has waited his whole life for this."
  "Give the finished Bill of Health to Pike at the gate."
tip if act 3 and has calendar_leaf and has bill
  nudge "A day off Pike's calendar, and a bill that wants dating."
  "Use the calendar leaf on the Bill of Health."
tip if act 3 and has bill and not bill_smoked
  nudge "Regulation three: a bill is fumigated first. Pike keeps a little brazier for it."
  "Use the Bill of Health on the fumigation brazier beside the gate."
tip if act 3 and has bill and not bill_stamped
  nudge "The bill wants a harbour officer's stamp. You're a clerk of the customs house."
  "Use the harbour stamp on the Bill of Health."
tip if act 3 and has bill and not bill_signed
  nudge "The bill wants a ship's officer's signature, and there's a navigator on this island."
  "Give the Bill of Health to Quill to countersign."
tip if act 3 and has bill and pike_reading
  nudge "Pike is reciting regulation six with his eyes shut. His hut is open."
  "Pike's eyes are shut: pick up the calendar in his hut."
tip if act 3 and has bill and not bill_dated
  nudge "The date comes off the station calendar in Pike's hut, and Pike never takes his eyes off it. Almost never."
  "Ask Pike what regulation six is, then take the calendar from his hut while he recites."
tip if act 3 and log_read
  nudge "The quarantine runs on forms. Every captain carries blank ones, and your father never threw paper away."
  "Pick up a blank Bill of Health from the pigeonholes on the desk in the Arcadia's cabin."
tip if act 3 and hatch_open
  nudge "The hatch is open, and below it is your father's cabin."
  "Go down the hatch and read your father's log on the desk."
tip if act 3
  nudge "The way into the Arcadia is the hatch on her deck, and it's swollen shut. You packed for this."
  "Use the crowbar on the jammed hatch on the wreck's deck."
# Act IV
tip if act 4 and ledger_written and not iou_paid
  nudge "The book is right. Somebody is waiting on the pier, and somebody in the Keel has a debt to settle."
  "Go back to the docks and talk to Quill on the pier. Sea or desk? (Optional first: Bramwick has a debt to settle in the Keel, and the steps to Upper Town are open.)"
tip if act 4 and ledger_written
  nudge "The book is right. Quill is waiting on the pier, and somebody up the steps asked to be told."
  "Go back to the docks and talk to Quill on the pier. Sea or desk? (Optional first: the steps to Upper Town are open, and somebody up there asked to be told.)"
tip if act 4 and quarantine_lifted and not iou_paid
  nudge "The flag is down and the stamp is back in your hand. One entry in the harbour ledger still says lost."
  "Use the harbour stamp on the harbour ledger, in the Salty Keel. (Optional: talk to Bramwick there; he has a debt to pay.)"
tip if act 4 and quarantine_lifted
  nudge "One entry in the harbour ledger still says lost, and the whole Keel is watching."
  "Use the harbour stamp on the harbour ledger, in the Salty Keel."
tip if act 4 and inquiry_done
  nudge "Bramwick is reinstated in everything but his stamp, and only his stamp lifts the yellow flag."
  "Give the harbour stamp back to Bramwick in the Salty Keel."
tip if act 4 and has ledger and has purse and has claims_book
  nudge "The ledger, the purse, the claims book. Cray is at the Keel, toasting the Marrow's memory."
  "You have the evidence. Talk to Cray in the Salty Keel and hold your inquiry."
tip if act 4 and has requisition and req_stamped
  nudge "Nib never reads anything. He looks for a stamp, and now there is one."
  "Give the stamped requisition to Nib in the counting house."
tip if act 4 and has requisition
  nudge "Nib looks for the stamp, not the words."
  "Use the harbour stamp on the requisition."
tip if act 4 and seen:nib.claims2 and not has claims_book
  nudge "Nib gives nothing to people, only to requisitions."
  "Pick up a requisition from the tray on Nib's desk."
tip if act 4 and seen:bramwick4.paper and not purse_given
  nudge "“A man who was there when it happened.” He's in the Keel, at the corner table, pretending not to listen."
  "Talk to Old Rook in the Salty Keel: tell him his captain is alive."
tip if act 4 and seen:bramwick4.paper and not ledger_taken
  nudge "Bramwick's own ledger, with his own lie in it, is still chained to its desk in the loft."
  "The ledger is in the loft above Chandler's Lane. Use the crowbar on it to break its chain."
tip if act 4 and seen:bramwick4.paper and not has claims_book
  nudge "Whatever Cray's counting house keeps on its insurance. The counting house is up Chandler's Lane."
  "Cray & Co. is up Chandler's Lane. Ask Nib, the clerk, for the insurance claims book."
tip if act 4 and farewell
  nudge "Cray has Bramwick's chair. Bramwick is drinking at the Keel, and he knows his regulations."
  "Talk to Bramwick in the Salty Keel: ask how to get him reinstated."
tip if act 4
  nudge "The Marrow is anchored past the boom, and Quill is at her rail."
  "Talk to Quill on the Marrow's rail (the ship on the left)."
